\finish is not a command on its own, calling it results in
an "unknown command" error. Finishing a piece is done with
the finish method of \score:

\score.finish

This makes the sequencer stop at the end of the loop that
is currently playing, and marks the end of the score, also
in any connected LiveLily-part programs.
It takes no arguments.

To stop at the start of the next bar instead, use
\score.stop, and to stop immediately, use \score.stopnow.
See also the help file of \score.
